# What Vercel uploads, and what it must not.
#
# The important line is .env. It is gitignored, so it is not in the repository --
# but Vercel uploads the *directory*, not the git tree, so a local .env full of
# real keys would be shipped to the build. VITE_-prefixed values in it would then
# be inlined into the client bundle, which is the difference between a private key
# and a published one. Excluding the directory is the only thing that guarantees it.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
dist
.vercel

# Not needed to build or run, and together they are a third of the upload.
scripts
tests
*.log

# Working notes. Worth keeping in git, not worth shipping to a build.
RULES.md

# Screenshots and scratch output from local verification.
shots
*.png
!src/assets/*.png
